From f547e59bb57f28e1b102314c083329e92ffa5a5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:45:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Match Firefox for Android (Fenix) on narrow windows

Make desktop Firefox behave like Fenix on phone-sized windows (700 CSS px
wide or less), each piece following Fenix's own sources:

- Extension popups open as full-height sheets with an app bar (back,
  extension name), refit when the on-screen keyboard opens and closes,
  and close when their toolbar button is tapped again.
- Android's content prefs: (hover: none) / (pointer: coarse), meta
  viewport, and the rest of geckoview-prefs.js that applies on Linux.
- Long-press context menu as Fenix's centred dialog with Fenix's items.
- No hover highlights on touch; no status panel.
- Tab counter: long-press menu, toolbar swipes to switch tabs, swipe up
  or tap for the tab tray (grid or list, multi-select, swipe to close,
  undo, private tabs, recently closed).
- App menu in Fenix's order.
- Find in page bar at the bottom with an n/N counter.
- Toolbar hides on scroll (Gecko's dynamic toolbar through
  InspectorUtils), pull to refresh with SwipeRefreshLayout's behaviour.
- Download prompt dialog and download snackbars instead of the
  downloads panel; snackbars for bookmarks, closed tabs and copied
  links.
- <select> as Fenix's choice dialog (single and multiple).
- Site permission prompts as Fenix's bottom sheet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXjPGasJxD6XRYU1J9jsnW
