+/**
+ * The tab tray of Firefox for Android (Fenix "tab manager"): a full-screen
+ * sheet with a private / normal page switcher, the tabs as a grid (or a
+ * list), a floating three-dot menu and a "+" button. Opened by tapping the
+ * tab counter and by swiping the toolbar away from the screen edge.
+ *
+ * Fenix sources (mobile/android/fenix/.../tabstray/ui/):
+ *   banner/TabsTrayBanner.kt    48dp row of page buttons, indicator under the
+ *                               selected one, multi-select banner
+ *   tabstray/TabsTray.kt        Scaffold: banner, pager, floating toolbar
+ *   tabpage/TabLayout.kt        grid (2 columns from 320dp, 3 from 480dp, 4
+ *                               from 800dp; 16dp gaps, 16/24dp padding) or
+ *                               list (16dp padding); gridTabView defaults to
+ *                               true in Settings.kt
+ *   tabitems/TabGridTabItem.kt  card with 12dp favicon, title, 40dp close
+ *                               button, thumbnail; aspect ratio 0.8
+ *   tabitems/TabListTabItem.kt  78x68dp thumbnail, title (2 lines), url,
+ *                               48dp close button
+ *   fab/TabManagerFloatingToolbar.kt  56dp pill with the menu, FAB, the menu
+ *                               items and the "Close all tabs?" dialog
+ *   tabpage/EmptyTabPage.kt, NormalTabsPage.kt, PrivateTabsPage.kt
+ * Strings are Fenix's strings.xml.
+ *
+ * Differences that come from desktop Firefox: private tabs live in their own
+ * windows, so the private page lists the tabs of the private windows and its
+ * "+" opens a tab in one. Synced tabs, tab groups, tab search, collections
+ * and inactive tabs are not here.
